# Base URL of the JurisCore API. No trailing slash.
#
# Leave this UNSET for local development. The application calls the API with relative
# paths (`/api/v1/...`), and the Vite dev server proxies those to Spring Boot on
# http://localhost:8080 — see `server.proxy` in vite.config.ts. Nothing else is needed.
#
# If your backend listens somewhere else, point the *proxy* at it rather than setting the
# variable below, so requests stay same-origin and CORS stays out of the picture:
#
#   VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:9090 npm run dev
#
# Set VITE_API_BASE_URL only for a deployed frontend served from a different origin than
# the API, e.g.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.juriscore.example
#
# That origin must appear in the backend's JURISCORE_CORS_ORIGINS allow-list.
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach the browser, and everything that does is public:
# it is compiled into the bundle. Never put a secret, key or token in this file.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
